      "text": "where we use that tmfQ is the free E∞-Q-algebra on two generators c4 and c6 in degrees 8 and 12, respectively, that TMFQ ≃ tmfQ[∆−1] for ∆ = (c34 − c26)/1728, and that the containment above is a monomorphism onto those path components where the image of ∆ is invertible. Both the base-change of T and TQ to ( p B)Q are chosen such that the associated map from tmfQ sends c4 and c6 to their q-expansion maps. From the equivalences above, this shows that these oriented elliptic curves are equivalent over ( p B)Q. The fact that ( p B)Q has homotopy groups concentrated in even degrees also shows that the choice of equivalence is unique up to homotopy; even up to 3-homotopy. This yields the oriented elliptic curve T over B.",
